:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Lake Solo []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'lake_ruin'>><<underwater>><<effects>><<lakeeffects>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    You force your attention onto the rope.
    The phantom chain bites into your palms, then softens one knot at a time.
    You pull until the ruined wall becomes stone again, then follow the knots towards the surface.
  <<option 'CN'>>
    你迫使自己专注于绳索。
    幻象中的铁链割痛手掌，又随着一个个绳结逐渐变回柔软的绳子。
    你不断拉动绳索，直到坍塌的墙壁重新变回石头，随后沿着绳结返回水面。
<</language>>
<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
<<swimicon 'up'>><<lanLink '返回湖岸' 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Lake Return' >><</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Lake Return []
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to 'lake'>><<effects>><<lakeeffects>>
<<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
  <<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<</if>>
<<set $_historyKylarCompromised to $LifeSimulation.historyProject.kylar is 'sabotage' and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.kylarStreet and !$LifeSimulation.historyProject.kylarPrepared >>
<<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin to $LifeSimulation.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and !$_historyKylarCompromised ? 2 : 1 >>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Back on the shore, you seal the golden statuette inside its padded pouch
    and lay the wet slates out beneath the trees.
    <br><br>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and !$_historyKylarCompromised>>
      Your position sketch,
      measurements and recovery notes remain legible.
      <br><br>
      <span class="green">You know where the statuette was lying, and you wrote it down in time.</span>
    <<elseif $_historyKylarCompromised>>
      Robin corrected the altered route,
      but the detour disturbed the entrance before you could record it.
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">The statuette is genuine, though part of its context has been lost.</span>
    <<else>>
      The statuette survived, but the disturbed silt makes its original position difficult to prove.
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">The recovery record remains incomplete.</span>
    <</if>>
    <<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
      <br><br>
      Robin copies the fading measurements onto dry paper while you redraw the chamber.
        When <<person1>><<his>> hand begins to shake, <<he>> presses it against yours until both are steady.
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    回到湖岸后，你把金制女祭司像封进内衬软垫的回收袋，
    又将湿透的记录板摊在树下。
    <br><br>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded' and !$_historyKylarCompromised >>你的位置草图、测量数据
      和回收记录仍然清晰可辨。
      <br><br>
      <span class="green">你记下了女祭司像原本躺着的位置，而且赶在痕迹消失之前。</span>
    <<elseif $_historyKylarCompromised>>
      罗宾修正了被篡改的路线，
      绕路却在记录前搅乱了入口处的淤泥。
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">女祭司像本身确为真品，部分出土环境却已经丢失。</span>
    <<else>>
      女祭司像完好无损，但被搅动的淤泥使原本位置难以证实。
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">这份回收记录仍不完整。</span>
    <</if>>
    <<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
      <br><br>
      你重画石室时，罗宾趁测量数据消退前，把它们誊写到干纸上。
        <<person1>><<his>>手指开始发抖时，<<he>>把手压在你的手上，直到两人都稳定下来。
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<lakeicon>><<lanLink '返回湖岸' 'Lake Shore'>>
  <<endevent>>
<</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'home'>><<effects>>
<<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
  <<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      You arrange the raid records,
      early catalogue cards and paint observations across the floor.
      The town's bombing is well documented. The painting's shifting colours are visible.
      Neither proves that its unknown artist predicted the red moons that followed.
    <<else>>
      You arrange the old catalogue cards, translations of the frame inscription
      and the painting's condition record across the floor.
      The object is centuries old. The tale attached to it changes from one telling to the next.
      Nothing you found turns one of those versions into an eyewitness account.
    <</if>>
    <br><br>
    <<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
      Robin trims labels and pins them beside the cards.
        "This one says what the catalogue wrote," <<he>> says, passing you a card.
        "This one says what people kept saying. They shouldn't look the same."
    <<else>>
      With the cards laid out beside the frame and the damage, you can see where your notes end
        and somebody else's version begins.
    <</if>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      <br><br>
      Your forest-lake sketches and the statuette's recovery record sit in a separate folder.
      They make a striking fieldwork sidebar, but they do not supply a missing chapter in the painting's history.
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      你把空袭记录、早期目录卡
      和颜料观察笔记铺满地板。
      城镇遭受轰炸一事有充分记录，画作变幻的颜色也肉眼可见。
      两者都不能证明，无名画家曾预言后来出现的红月。
    <<else>>
      你把旧目录卡、画框题名译文和画作状况记录铺满地板。
      实物确有数百年历史，附着其上的故事却在每次讲述中变化。
      你找到的东西中，没有一样能把某个版本变成亲历记录。
    <</if>>
    <br><br>
    <<if maplebirch.get('LifeSimulation').school.historyAssistantAvailable>>
      罗宾裁好标签，把它们钉在卡片旁。
        “这张写目录上原本怎么写的，”<<he>>说道，把一张卡递给你，
        “那张写大家后来一直在说什么。它们不该看起来完全一样。”
    <<else>>
      卡片和画框、损伤并排摊开后，你能一眼看出哪几行到你的笔记为止，
        哪几行已经是别人添上去的版本。
    <</if>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      <br><br>
      森林湖草图和女祭司像的回收记录被你放进另一只文件夹。
      它们可以组成醒目的实地调查侧栏，却无法填补画作历史中缺失的一章。
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<historyicon>><<lanLink ['Hang only what the cards support', '只挂有据可查的部分'] 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish' >><<set $phase to 0>><</lanLink>><<ghistory>><br>
<<historyicon>><<lanLink ['Fill the gaps with the best story', '用最精彩的说法补上缺口'] 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish' >><<set $phase to 1>><</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Draft Finish []
<<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.draft to $phase is 0 ? 25 : 12>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $phase is 0>>
      <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
        Your first panels reconstruct
        the documented raid and the painting's route back to the museum.
        The last separates its unusual pigment from the prediction later attached to it.
      <<else>>
        Your first panels establish the painting's age, title and damage.
        The last traces how incompatible versions gathered around the same image.
      <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <span class="green">Your exhibition is ready.</span>
    <<else>>
      You join the gaps with the most dramatic version available.
      The display flows cleanly, so long as nobody asks which labels describe records
      and which describe your preferred story.
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">Your exhibition is ready.</span><<famesocial 1>>
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $phase is 0>>
      <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
        前几块展板复原有记录的空袭，
        以及画作辗转回到博物馆的经历。最后一块则把异常颜料与后来附会的预言分开。
      <<else>>
        前几块展板说明画作的年代、题名与损伤，
        最后一块则追踪彼此冲突的故事如何逐渐汇聚到同一幅画上。
      <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <span class="green">你的展览已经准备完成。</span>
    <<else>>
      你用最富戏剧性的版本填平了所有空缺。
      整场展览显得十分流畅，前提是没人追问哪些标签来自记录，
      哪些只是你最中意的故事。
      <br><br>
      <span class="teal">你的展览已经准备完成。</span><<famesocial 1>>
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br><<homeicon>><<lanLink ['Put the project away', '收好项目'] 'Bedroom'>><</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Exhibition []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'museum'>><<effects>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Your display occupies one wall of the museum.
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      The red-moon painting hangs above
      a timeline of the raid, its return to the collection and the claims later attached to it.
    <<else>>
      The snake-woman painting hangs above its translated title,
      condition record and a branching map of the tale's incompatible versions.
    <</if>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gte 2>>
      A smaller case to one side contains the golden priestess statuette,
      your position sketch and a plainly labelled field note.
      The sketch still shows where she was lying when you found her.
    <<elseif $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      A smaller case to one side contains the golden priestess statuette and your field note.
      The note admits that the statuette's original position was disturbed before you could fix it.
    <</if>>
  <br><br>
  Winter waits until the room quiets. A visitor leans in to hear.
    "One question," <<he>> says.
    "Which of these labels would you defend, and which would you take down?"
  <<option 'CN'>>
    你的展览占据了博物馆的一整面墙。
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
      红月画作悬在展板上方，
      下方的时间线依次列出空袭、画作回归藏品，以及后来附着其上的种种说法。
    <<else>>
      蛇女画作悬在展板上方，下面依次展示题名译文、状况记录，
      以及一张向外分岔的图表，梳理彼此冲突的故事版本。
    <</if>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gte 2>>
      侧边另有一只较小的展柜，放着金制女祭司像、
      位置草图，以及明确标注为实地记录的说明。
      草图上还留着你就地画下的、她原本躺着的位置。
    <<elseif $LifeSimulation.historyProject.ruin gt 0>>
      侧边另有一只较小的展柜，放着金制女祭司像和你的实地记录。
      记录里说明，你还没来得及固定位置，那片淤泥就已经被搅动了。
    <</if>>
  <br><br>
  温特等房间安静下来。一名参观者凑近了些。
    “最后一个问题。”<<he>>说道，
    “这些标签里，哪几块你愿意替它辩护，哪几块你会亲手摘下来？”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<set $_historyCorrectAnswer to $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward' ? lanSwitch( 'Say the painting was there, and later people decided what it meant', '画就在那里，是后来的人替它定下了含义' ) : lanSwitch( 'Say the painting is old, but the story about it is not', '画是旧的，画上的故事不是' ) >>
<<historyicon>><<link $_historyCorrectAnswer 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result' >>
  <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final to 15>>
  <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.archive + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.museum + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.draft + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final is 100 >>
    <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status to 'won'>>
  <<else>>
    <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
  <</if>>
<</link>><<ghistory>><br>
<<museumicon>><<lanLink ['Trust the painting\'s age', '相信画作年代'] 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result' >>
  <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final to 0>>
  <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
<</lanLink>><br>
<<historyicon>><<lanLink ['Trust the repeated account', '相信流传最广的说法'] 'Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result' >>
  <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final to 0>>
  <<set $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status to 'done'>>
<</lanLink>><br>

:: Deadwood Reblooms History Project Result []
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to 'museum'>><<effects>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<if ['done', 'won'].includes($LifeSimulation.historyProject.status) and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.archive is 30 and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.museum is 30 and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.draft is 25 and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final is 15 and $LifeSimulation.historyProject.recovery is 'recorded'>>
  <<earnFeat 'Evidence Matters'>>
<</if>>
<<set $_historyScore to $LifeSimulation.historyProject.archive + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.museum + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.draft + $LifeSimulation.historyProject.final >>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status is 'won'>>
      "Exactly," Winter says.
        <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
          "The raid is in the town records. The paint is on the canvas.
          What is left over is what people wanted the painting to mean."
        <<else>>
          "An old frame, an old canvas, an old grudge.
          That is the whole of it. The rest is other people's handwriting."
        <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <<He>> turns to the visitors.
        "The exhibit holds because it stops where the paperwork stops."
        The questions that follow are directed to you rather than Winter.
        <span class="green">You answer each one without needing to look at your notes.</span>
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 75>>
      Winter studies your display before nodding.
        "<span class="green">Not bad.</span> Two of these labels are guessing. A visitor will find them."
        <br><br>
        The visitors remain to examine your reconstruction.
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 50>>
      "This is a <span class="teal">good story</span>," Winter says.
        "Next time, separate it from the cards before you put it on a wall."
        <br><br>
        <<He>> leaves your display open for the afternoon.
    <<else>>
      Winter corrects several labels while the visitors move on.
        "<span class="red">You wrote half of this yourself</span>," <<he>> says quietly.
        "The museum catalogues would like a word."
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.status is 'won'>>
      “完全正确。”温特说道，
        <<if $LifeSimulation.historyProject.source is 'paintingward'>>
          “空袭记在镇子的档案里，颜料就在画布上。
          剩下的部分，是后人希望这幅画意味着什么。”
        <<else>>
          “旧画框、旧画布、一桩旧怨。
          全部就这些。其余的，是别人的笔迹。”
        <</if>>
      <br><br>
      <<He>>转向参观者。
        “这场展览站得住，是因为它在档案停下的地方也停下了。”
        接下来的问题全都抛向你，而非温特。<span class="green">你不必查看笔记，便逐一作出回答。</span>
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 75>>
      温特审视展板片刻，随后点了点头。
        “<span class="green">还行。</span>这两块是猜的。参观者会揪出来。”
      <br><br>
      参观者仍留在原地，继续查看你的复原图。
    <<elseif $_historyScore gte 50>>
      “这是个<span class="teal">好故事</span>。”温特说道，
        “下次记得先把它和目录卡分开，再挂到墙上。”
      <br><br>
      <<He>>让你的展览继续开放了一下午。
    <<else>>
      参观者逐渐离开，温特则亲手修正了几张标签。
        “<span class="red">这里一半是你自己编的</span>。”<<he>>低声说道，
        “博物馆的目录不会同意。”
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<br><br><<museumicon>><<lanLink '返回博物馆' 'Museum'>><</lanLink>><br>

:: Museum Golden Priestess Statuette []
<<effects>><<museumClearHint 'antiquegoldpriestess'>><<npc Winter>><<person1>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    Winter studies the statuette's kneeling robes and the script around its base through the glass.
    "A priestess making an offering," <<he>> says. "Not a soldier."
    <br><br>
    "The gold is the least interesting part. Where you found it is the important thing.
      Same script as the forest sanctuary, same temple. Old, and not originally ours.
      It still won't tell you why the place went under."
  <<option 'CN'>>
    温特隔着玻璃，仔细观察女祭司像跪伏的长袍与底座周围的文字。
    “正在奉上供物的女祭司。”<<he>>说道，“不是士兵。”
    <br><br>
    “黄金是最没意思的部分。你是在哪儿找到它的，这才是关键。
      和森林里那座礼拜场所一样的字形，同一座神殿。年头很久，本来也不属于我们。
      它还是不会告诉你，那地方为什么会沉下去。”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<museumicon>><<lanLink '返回博物馆' 'Museum'>><<endevent>><</lanLink>><br>
